Third-party headers in gdbgui/static/engine/include/

1. GCC libstdc++ policy-based data structures and helpers
   Files: ext/pb_ds/** (243 files), ext/typelist.h, ext/type_traits.h, ext/numeric_traits.h,
          bits/cpp_type_traits.h, bits/version.h
   Source: https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc, libstdc++-v3/include/, commit
           ee5bf81d7816b0b6c54788f195295ba448cda49e (2026-09-25), copied unmodified
           (same files the E1 experiment validated; see experiments/frontend-only/e1/REPORT.md, E1c).
   License: GNU GPL v3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1 (COPYING3, COPYING.RUNTIME in
            this directory). The original license headers are kept in every file.

2. vgdb's own compatibility layer (part of this repository, GPL-3.0-or-later like gdbgui):
   bits/stdc++.h, bits/extc++.h, bits/c++config.h, debug/debug.h, tr1/functional, tr1/type_traits,
   vgcompat.h (from experiments/frontend-only/e1/mine, plus vgcompat.h added in S1).

The wasm toolchain (clang/lld/sysroot, LLVM Apache-2.0 with LLVM exception; wasi-libc MIT/BSD;
browsercc MIT) is not stored in the repository: it is installed by `npm ci` and copied into the
git-ignored assets/ directory by scripts/build-assets.mjs. Only browsercc's emscripten JS glue is
vendored in vendor/browsercc/ together with its MIT LICENSE.
